Devil sprite pack — Little Voices stage renderer port

Adapted from Jon Taylor's Little Voices, https://github.com/pipecat-ai/ios-little-voices,
revision 7f5613cd9071d4668d3aab9cfe8691ff8c59b4b2. Copyright (c) 2026 Daily; BSD-2.

Read/ported source: FaceRig.swift, FaceGeometry.swift, FaceExpressions.swift,
FaceParameters.swift, RigMath.swift, DuoCharacter.swift, DuoStageView.swift,
StageRenderer.swift, StageLayout.swift, StageColors.swift, StagePalette.swift,
GlowSprites.swift, SeamRig.swift, LipsyncVisemes.swift. The source renderer's
settled paths, gradient stops, stroke widths, eye clips, brow tapers, cavity,
tongue, fang and hinged accessories are evaluated in ../little-voices.cjs.
The single-character adaptation omits the two-character seam/captions and live
spring simulation. A fixed full-stage crop fits the round display; no face disc.

Build: node assets/characters/devil/build-sprites.cjs (from repository root).
Dependencies: Node, Python3 with Pillow, system librsvg-2 and Cairo. The build
uses procedural SVG only; reference images are comparison inputs, never sprite
inputs. ../duo-raster.py uses fixed 2x sampling and straight-alpha PNG output.
Glow shadows use two Gaussian passes; the CoreGraphics blur kernel differs.

Animation v2: full-canvas gradient faceplate, seven tightly bounded eyes/brows
frames (including true app neutral), five mouth frames. The app's neutral angel
has bead eyes; open uses its surprised white-eye parameters to match the brief.
Devil open uses talking eyes looking toward the other character. Side looks
include the app's settled parallax. All combinations remain independently valid.

Rest mouth is the app's neutral open smile/grin. Speaking frames small, medium,
wide, round are exact LipSyncMapping samples at talkOpen .25, .5, .75, 1 with
width .5 and rounding .1. The legacy round filename now stores the maximum
opening, not an O; this keeps the devil fang in every pack mouth. Energy-based
animation is not phoneme alignment. Halo/horns, blush and marks remain static.
Restore dirty union from the faceplate and redraw intersecting patches in order.

Previews/fidelity: python3 hil/duo_art_rev1.py --out ~/src/evidence/duo/step-1-rev-1
Host checks: TMPDIR=$HOME/.cache/gap3-tmp PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 -m unittest hil/test_duo_art_rev1.py -v
The revision suite retains original determinism/transition/decoder checks and
replaces the solid-field-only safety assertion with separate feature safety.
User art approval and on-device validation remain pending.

