The procedural drawing ports proportions, curves, expressions and colours from
FaceGeometry.swift, FaceExpressions.swift, FaceParameters.swift, StageColors.swift
and StagePalette.swift. Changes: a single round-safe 412px face, flat fills in
place of gradients/glows, six eye/brow patches and five energy-driven mouth poses.
The shared rasterizer is ../duo-build.cjs. No image-generation service is used.

Build: node assets/characters/devil/build-sprites.cjs (from repository root).
Export estimates and previews: python3 hil/duo_art.py --out ~/src/evidence/duo/step-1
Preview export needs Pillow; PNG builds use only Node's standard library.
Host acceptance: TMPDIR=$HOME/.cache/gap3-tmp PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 -m unittest hil/test_duo_art.py -v

Animation schema v2 follows the Halloween cat: faceplate plus transparent,
union-bounded eyes-with-brows and mouth patches. Coordinates are authored at 412;
runtime estimates use endpoint-rounded 360 coordinates. Restore dirty bounds
from the faceplate before compositing patches, including other intersecting
layers. Transparent RGB is zero; partial alpha is straight, not premultiplied.
Optional accents are omitted; the halo/horns and marks are static faceplate art.

User approval of the art and on-device validation remain pending. Estimates and
preview GIFs are external evidence, not installed runtime assets.

